==Trivia==
*The word "''Prince''" comes from the Latin word "''prīnceps''", meaning first head.
**The Dark Prince is 1 of 20 [[cards]] associated with nobility, with the others being [[Knight]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Royal Giant]], [[Royal Delivery]], [[Tower Princess]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Prince]], [[Raging Prince]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Princess]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Spirit Empress]], [[Super Knight]], [[Dagger Duchess]], [[Royal Chef]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], and the [[Little Prince]].
*Shields were first developed during the Bronze Age, as a protection device, designed to block attacks by hand weapons, such as swords, axes and maces, or ranged weapons like sling-stones and arrows. Shields have varied greatly in construction over time and place. Sometimes shields were made of metal, but wood or animal hide construction was much more common; wicker and even turtle shells have been used. Shields were retired in warfare, but are still used to this day for police enforcement.
**The Dark Prince is 1 of 3 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] to have a shield, along with the Royal Recruits and [[Guards]].
*The Dark Prince's pony resembles a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shetland_pony Shetland pony], a breed of ponies that has a compact body with short legs and a long mane, and is commonly ridden in horse shows.
*He is 1 of 5 troops that have a charge, the others being [[Battle Ram]], Prince, Raging Prince, and [[Ram Rider]].
*The Dark Prince is 1 of 8 troops that can jump over the river, the others being [[Hog Rider]], Royal Hogs, Prince, Raging Prince, Ram Rider, [[Mother Witch|Cursed Hog]], and [[Santa Hog Rider]].
*The Prince and the Dark Prince are revealed to be brothers according to the balance changes in the [[Version History#Tournaments%20Update%20(4/7/2016)|Tournaments Update]].
*Similar to the Prince, once he starts charging, a sound effect will play. However, the Dark Prince's audio is muffled and played in a lower pitch compared to the Prince. 
**When the Dark Prince charges, he will shout "''Attack''" or "''Charge''".
***The Dark Prince is 1 of 24 troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Wizard]], Hog Rider, [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Bowler]], Ram Rider, [[Electro Wizard]], Princess, [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Lumberjack]], Mother Witch, [[Fisherman]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], Santa Hog Rider, [[Super Magic Archer]], Golden Knight, [[Boss Bandit]], Archer Queen, Little Prince, and the [[Terry]].
*From the Royal Recruits' description, it is implied that they can be promoted to be Dark Princes at some point.
*The Royal Recruits are commanded by the Dark Prince, as seen in a [https://www.facebook.com/ClashRoyale/posts/introducing-the-royal-recruits-/2116688775069410/ Facebook post].
*In [[w:c:Squad-Busters|Squad Busters]], the [[w:c:squad-busters:Pi%C3%B1ata|Piñata]] resembles a piñata version of the Dark Prince's pony.
*While not available as a character, the Dark Prince's sounds, along with the Knight, [[Barbarians]], and Wizard, are featured in the [[w:c:beatstar:Clash Royale Theme|Clash Royale Theme]] [[w:c:beatstar:Songs|song]] in Beatstar.
*When the Dark Prince is defeated, his spiked club falls to the ground. The other units that drop items upon death are the Knight, [[Rascals|Rascal Boy]], Mega Minion, [[Executioner]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Sparky]], Fisherman, Super Knight, Golden Knight, and the Little Prince.
*The Dark Prince is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Dark Prince is the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
**The Dark Prince is the subject of 4 [[Emotes]].
*The back of the Dark Prince's head can be seen without his bucket in the [https://youtu.be/SfoPTgt4jXs?si=F3qJjcyjbE2PL-NI&t=38 Little Prince release video].
**The "On The Road Again" [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] shows the front of his face.

